cla_mmrs: describe how the CLA debug interrupt is released

A debug-interrupt action holds the interrupt while EnableEap is set: the
node's action-bus idle value feeds the interrupt back every cycle, and the
top-level latch gives the set priority over the CDbgEapStatus w2c clear.
A w2c write therefore clears only the status bit. Clearing EnableEap stops
the hold, and the next w2c write releases the line. This is the intended
behaviour, and CDbgEapStatus and EnableEap now say so.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
index c6a575f4c..96905d092 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
@@ -3211,7 +3211,10 @@ c_dbg_eap_status:
       per EAP in bits [15:0] (Node0Eap0..Node3Eap3, 4 EAPs per Node across 4 Nodes) and
       one write-to-clear bit per EAP in bits [47:32] (Node0Eap0W2C..Node3Eap3W2C); write
       the matching w2c bit to reset a status bit. The register is used by SW to know if an
-      action was taken (ex: NMI ISR needs to know which of the EAP triggered the NMI)'
+      action was taken (ex: NMI ISR needs to know which of the EAP triggered the NMI).
+      A w2c write does not release a debug interrupt while EnableEap is set: the EAP
+      holds the interrupt and the write clears only the status bit. To release it, clear
+      EnableEap, then write the w2c bit.'
     RESET_PORT: reset_n_warm_ovrride
     HW_READ: CLA
     HW_WRITE: CLA
@@ -3614,7 +3617,9 @@ c_dbg_cla_ctrl_status:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '5:5'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: Set Enable EAP to 1 after EAP programming is complete
+    DESCRIPTION: Set Enable EAP to 1 after EAP programming is complete. Clearing it
+      disables every EAP, and is required before the CDbgEapStatus w2c write that
+      releases a debug interrupt; set it again to re-arm the EAPs
     RESET_PORT: ''
     SW_WRITE: W
